                    {
                        "sense_id": "234d3e54-4d92-34cd-845a-200987083925",
                        "entry_id": "6f008427-0a44-36aa-89cc-c85e097528fd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An academy for the advanced study of Jewish texts."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Judaism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "65ac2c55-78cd-48f2-8c21-842e05708b6e",
                                "sense_id": "234d3e54-4d92-34cd-845a-200987083925",
                                "text": "Nonetheless, in 1976, after graduating with a B.A. in religious studies, he entered Yale's doctoral program in the same department. A year later, he left Yale to study Talmud in a Manhattan yeshiva."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ed9ffed-b312-4dfa-92e7-72fc70ac8861",
                                "sense_id": "234d3e54-4d92-34cd-845a-200987083925",
                                "text": "Shalom grew up in an Orthodox family in Stamford Hill. His father, who ran an office-furniture business, intended him for a synagogue cantor, and when Shalom finished school he was sent to the yeshiva."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "987d752d-76b5-4292-8f4c-1ad6c9586811",
                                "sense_id": "234d3e54-4d92-34cd-845a-200987083925",
                                "text": "Last month, the Forward reported, a former student at Mechon Hadar—a co-ed egalitarian yeshiva in New York—emailed the school's listserv with a plea for the institution to cut ties with [Leslie] Wexner in light of the unspooling allegations against [Jeffrey] Epstein."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "20f4824f-931a-4cd2-968e-ada495066a66",
                        "source_entry_id": "6f008427-0a44-36aa-89cc-c85e097528fd",
                        "source_sense_id": "234d3e54-4d92-34cd-845a-200987083925",
                        "source_sense_description": "academy for the advanced study of Jewish texts",
                        "target_lang_word": "yeshiva",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "yeshiva",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b84ca6e-91de-39af-9712-779be862b367",
                                        "entry_id": "fcba0f4a-e3d4-331a-931b-6967dd605e3e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chez les juifs, établissement d’enseignement supérieur dans lequel l’étude du Talmud et de la Torah est continuelle et intensive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Judaism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83c45303-4fde-4b2b-ad72-5c7d96036092",
                                                "sense_id": "7b84ca6e-91de-39af-9712-779be862b367",
                                                "text": "On m’entraîna, le lendemain de Simhat Torah, dans la yeshiva du maître le plus vénéré alors, descendant d’une fondatrice lignée lituanienne — très vieux, il avait, par une chance extraordinaire, survécu à la Shoah."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6699d95-7e9f-4708-af0b-171bf60a083d",
                                                "sense_id": "7b84ca6e-91de-39af-9712-779be862b367",
                                                "text": "Il se retrouve pris dans le même mystère, dissèque les documents et les scrute avec la passion d’un théologien des premiers temps, d’un rabbin dans une yeshiva découvrant que chaque mot peut vouloir dire une chose et son contraire..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
